1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,640
Julie: Hello?

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:03,950
Greg: Oh, hello. Is that Julie Davison?

3
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:05,060
Julie: Yes.

4
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:08,300
Greg: This is Greg Preston from the Employment Agency.

5
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:12,980
We met last week when you came in to enquire about office work.

6
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:14,300
Julie: Oh, that's right.

7
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:19,670
Greg: Now we've just had some details come in of a job which might interest you.

8
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:20,640
Julie: OK.

9
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:24,680
Greg: So this is a position for a receptionist

10
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:28,270
I believe you've done that sort of work before?

11
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:34,800
Julie: Yes, I have, I worked in a sports centre for a couple of years before I got married and had the children.

12
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:40,360
Greg: Right. Well, this job's in Fordham, so not too far away for you

13
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:42,900
and it's at the medical centre there.

14
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:45,980
Julie: OK. So where exactly is that?

15
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:49,810
Greg: It's quite near the station, on Chastons Road.

16
00:00:49,810 --> 00:00:50,750
Julie: Sorry?

17
00:00:50,750 --> 00:01:02,090
Greg: Chastons Road - that's C-H-A-S-T-O-N-S.

18
00:01:02,090 --> 00:01:05,360
Julie: OK, thanks. So what would the work involve

19
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:07,920
Dealing with enquiries from patients?

20
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:12,400
Greg: Yes, and you'd also be involved in making appointments

21
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,312
whether face to face or on the phone.

22
00:01:16,312 --> 00:01:18,520
And rescheduling them if necessary.

23
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,710
Julie: Fine, that shouldn't be a problem.

24
00:01:20,710 --> 00:01:26,775
Greg: And another of your duties would be keeping the centre's database up-to-date.

25
00:01:26,775 --> 00:01:31,320
Then you might have other general administrative duties as well

26
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:34,140
but those would be the main ones.

27
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:35,440
Julie: OK.

28
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:37,760
Greg: Now when the details came in

29
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:42,958
I immediately thought of you because one thing they do require is someone

30
00:01:42,958 --> 00:01:48,520
with experience, and you did mention your work at the sports centre

31
00:01:48,520 --> 00:01:50,100
when you came in to see us.

32
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:55,580
Julie: Yes, in fact I enjoyed that job. Is there anything else they're looking for?

33
00:01:55,580 --> 00:02:02,203
Greg: Well, they say it's quite a high-pressure environment, they're always very busy,

34
00:02:02,203 --> 00:02:04,460
and patients are often under stress

35
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:10,151
so they want someone who can cope with that and stay calm,

36
00:02:10,151 --> 00:02:15,450
and at the same time be confident when interacting with the public.

37
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:18,740
Julie: Well, after dealing with three children all under five

38
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,810
I reckon I can cope with that.

39
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:22,540
Greg: I'm sure you can.

40
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:30,080
Greg: And then another thing they mention is that they're looking for someone with good IT skills...

41
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,410
Julie: Not a problem.

42
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:34,310
Greg: So you'd be interested in following this up?

43
00:02:34,310 --> 00:02:36,930
Julie: Sure. When would it start?

44
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:41,495
Greg: Well, they're looking for someone from the beginning of next month,

45
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:45,709
but I should tell you that this isn't a permanent job,

46
00:02:45,709 --> 00:02:50,626
it's temporary, so the contract would be just to the end of September.

47
00:02:50,626 --> 00:02:54,840
But they do say that there could be further opportunities after that.

48
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:57,890
Julie: OK. And what would the hours be?

49
00:02:57,890 --> 00:03:03,790
Greg: Well, they want someone who can start at a quarter to eight in the morning - could you manage that?

50
00:03:03,790 --> 00:03:08,579
Julie: Yes, my husband would have to get the kids up and off to my mother's -

51
00:03:08,579 --> 00:03:13,650
she's going to be looking after them while I'm at work. What time would I finish?

52
00:03:13,650 --> 00:03:14,940
Greg: One fifteen.

53
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:17,057
Julie: That should work out all right.

54
00:03:17,057 --> 00:03:22,802
I can pick the kids up on my way home, and then I'll have the afternoon with them.

55
00:03:22,802 --> 00:03:26,430
Oh, one thing... is there parking available for staff at the centre?

56
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:30,110
Greg: Yes, there is, and it's also on a bus route.

57
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:35,319
Julie: Right. Well, I expect I'll have the car but it's good to know that.

58
00:03:35,319 --> 00:03:37,770
OK, so where do I go from here?

59
00:03:37,770 --> 00:03:44,084
Greg: Well, if you're happy for me to do so, I'll forward your CV and references,

60
00:03:44,084 --> 00:03:48,860
and then the best thing would probably be for you to phone them

61
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:51,100
so they can arrange for an interview.

62
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:53,460
Julie: Great. Well thank you very much.

63
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:55,310
Greg: You're welcome. Bye now.

64
00:03:55,310 --> 00:03:56,340
Julie: Bye.
